# Gilded Ghoda: Saddle 1 is "Saddle only as a sorcery" (CR 702.171a), so in Bot1's beginning of combat step with Mother of Runes ready
# to tap it is refused. On turn 5 Bot1 saddles it in the main phase, it attacks while saddled and makes a Treasure, and that Treasure
# is sacrificed for one green mana (CR 111.10a): Bot2 took 2, and the Treasure is gone.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Gilded Ghoda
Mother of Runes
Island x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gilded Ghoda.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
! Bot1.Battlefield.Gilded Ghoda.Activate(Ability: Saddle)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Gilded Ghoda.Activate(Ability: Saddle)
Bot1.Choose(Mother of Runes)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Gilded Ghoda > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token.Activate(Color: Green)

